  "conclusions": {
    "observed": "All26 terminal/parked V2 cases stopped before production TRICERATOPS probability integrations. Their outcomes cannot establish statistical rejection or general unsuitability of the BOI population.",
    "main_bottleneck": "Native preparation/sampling and aperture-response integration; stellar/blend information also limits individual cases.",
    "rewrite_causality": "No same-input V1/V2 candidate comparison establishes that deletion of custom evidence/prior machinery reduced actual validation success. Removing custom evidence kernels does not remove need for correct Kepler extraction/dilution inputs.",
    "core_verification": "Previously recorded Kepler10b direct upstream control had zero evidence/probability difference over15scenarios at32768draws. This tests API equivalence, not full faint/crowded own-SAP preparation or empirical reliability.",
    "protection_policy": "Native duration/clock allowed to vary but trend mask freezes recovered P/epoch/duration. Approximate coverage uses every predicted center between first/last sample, including gaps; percentage is not an observed-photon loss fraction. Posterior-tail overlap is a diagnostic, not an upstream universal zero-tolerance admission criterion. Some cases have large real overlap;7.19ppm/14.63ppm edge holds require proportionate review, not astrophysical rejection.",
    "aperture": "Pinned upstream uses fixed circular0.75pixel Gaussian. Existing calibrated-core checks normalize a limited capable-source group, not a complete measured scene. Renormalizing Gaussian to same group for saved previews leaves substantial discrepancies in several fields; normalization alone does not explain them. Applicability mismatch is not proof of bad candidates or a confirmed coordinate bug.",
    "bugs": "Pinned juliet2.2.10 evaluate_beta checks a>0,b<1 instead of x support, yielding-inf for Beta(.867,3.03) in emcee. Its emcee logprob also evaluates likelihood even when prior-inf. Separate nested batman solver failures are recorded with failed geometry unexported; their cause is not established and must not be attributed to the earlier emcee defect.",
    "recommended_focus": "Repair/review native preparation refinement and proportionate adequacy decisions, establish a defensible Kepler aperture-response path, then same-extraction known-object end-to-end checks. Preserve historical admissions and old failures; do not restore bespoke priors/kernels simply to obtain lower FPP."
